Build a local budget-and-actual dashboard — learner brief
Fictional Northstar Services training material.
Data contract
One row per unit/department/month; unique composite key. USD 000. Variance actual−budget. Synchronize unit filter, totals and detail table. No driver inference.
Task
Northstar wants an interactive view of a small fictional department budget table.
Actions
	1	State row grain, unique key, USD 000 units, and actual-minus-budget definition.
	2	Ask AI for a standalone dashboard with unit filter, totals, a simple comparison visual, and a complete detail table.
	3	Open the saved file and verify all-unit totals 350/360/+10.
	4	Select East and West and check both totals and visible rows against supplied expected results.
	5	Use keyboard-only navigation and ensure above-budget status has text or a sign, not color alone.
	6	Record source changes and any unresolved accessibility issue.
Output
Data contract; metric definitions; runnable source; filter test table; accessibility notes.
Supplied local practice files
	•	dashboard-starter.html
	•	invalid-currency.json
	•	invalid-duplicate.json
	•	invalid-missing.json
	•	october.json
	•	september.json
Keep these files together. Scripts take explicit paths; choose new output folders. Use a plain text editor to inspect source before running. Browser prototypes open locally; do not deploy them.
